#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198078 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f49ef1c2-06de-597c-bf4d-6d613989987e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Set Using a Conditional Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "cfd5a7b6-4ee8-5c66-9b1d-81d1d9a1aee7" :question/math-academy-id "e-13144" :question/problem "Describe the set $S = \\{-9,-8,-7, ..., 5\\}$ using a conditional definition." :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-9$ and $5$ (including $-9$ and $5$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS = \\{ x \\in \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\mathbb Z} \\: : \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-9} \\leq x \\leq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5} \\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example, we can write $S$ equivalently as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{ x \\in \\mathbb Z \\: : \\: -10 \\lt x \\lt 6 \\big\\}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198092 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9df722a8-2db6-5bb8-a69c-b81b33037ab2" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Given Set Using a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "e81a9a3f-3dbb-5244-8ea0-9b967bb5a46f" :question/math-academy-id "e-13184" :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\left\\{\\ldots, -36, -6, -1, -\\dfrac1{6}, -\\dfrac1{36}, ...\\right\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_1 = -\\dfrac16$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\\ldots,\\quad -36, \\quad -6, \\quad -1, \\quad -\\dfrac1{6}, \\quad -\\dfrac1{36}, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=\\dfrac16{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =(\\frac{-6}{-36}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-1}{-6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{6})}{(-1)} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  $a_1=-\\dfrac16,$ the $n$th term $a_n$ of our sequence for $n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{6})\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{6})\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{-1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{n} \\\\  & =-{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\left\\{-\\left(\\dfrac16\\right)^{n} \\: : \\: n\\in \\mathbb{Z}\\right\\}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198093 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad21350b-2e3b-57ee-a28c-32a7bd1b2513" :knowledge-point/title "Defining a Set Conditionally Using the Roots of a Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "a67f56bb-352b-5126-84c8-c38fc3d0532c" :question/math-academy-id "e-13185" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients $p$ and $q$ in the conditional definition of the set given below.\n\n$$\n\\{\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\\} = \\Big\\{z \\in \\mathbb{C} \\: : \\: 4z^2+pz+q = 0 \\Big\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $z\\in\\mathbb C$ of some quadratic polynomial $f(z).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots $z_1=-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (z-(-3\\text{i}))(z-(3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (z+3\\text{i})(z-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}-9{\\text{i}}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}+9) \\\\  & =4{z}^{2}+36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\\} = \\Big\\{z \\in \\mathbb{C} \\: : \\: 4z^2+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}z+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}36} = 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=0$ and $q=36.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198094 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c5b3eb6-187f-5f16-a32e-66b0842adfe9" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Given Set Using an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "231da77b-8370-543a-abf0-effb78e50802" :question/math-academy-id "e-13186" :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\{... , -5, -3, -1, 1, 3, ...\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_1 = 1$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\\ldots, \\quad -5, \\quad -3, \\quad -1, \\quad 1, \\quad 3, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =-3-(-5) \\\\  & =-1-(-3) \\\\  & =1-(-1) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  $a_1=1,$ the $n$th term $a_n$ of our sequence for $n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =1+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{2n-1 \\: : \\: n \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\big\\}\n$$\n\n**Watch Out!** \n\nThe constructive definition of a set is typically not unique. \n\nSince the elements of $A$ are generated by a *two-way* infinite arithmetic sequence, we could have picked *any* term in our sequence as $a_1$ when determining $a_n.$ We selected $a_1 = 1$ because this led to a nice, simple expression in our constructive definition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad21350b-2e3b-57ee-a28c-32a7bd1b2513" :knowledge-point/title "Defining a Set Conditionally Using the Roots of a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d56ff6-031c-5c97-9829-c17b0fa0efa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20d56ff6-031c-5c97-9829-c17b0fa0efa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305382} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fe06d7e-3cd9-5288-8190-6f570dd805db" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1de51858-6a53-5c48-be00-c31c73a12a57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1de51858-6a53-5c48-be00-c31c73a12a57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305381} :answer-field/id #uuid "13610ce8-a13d-5b0d-adbd-be1f7f021e9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "daeebfae-6abc-50c7-b86a-29781d3e20e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-181608" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${3,4}$ given below.\n\n${3,4}={n\\in Z\\,:\\,2{n}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$n\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $n\\in Z$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(n).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${n}_{1}=3$ and ${n}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(n) & =a(n-{n}_{1})(n-{n}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(n-3)(n-4) \\\\  & =2({n}^{2}-7n+12) \\\\  & =2{n}^{2}-14n+24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{3,4}={n\\in Z\\,:\\,2{n}^{2}-14n+24=0}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad21350b-2e3b-57ee-a28c-32a7bd1b2513" :knowledge-point/title "Defining a Set Conditionally Using the Roots of a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e9e4337-1c4b-5742-aeb5-bea0faeb5167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e9e4337-1c4b-5742-aeb5-bea0faeb5167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305384} :answer-field/id #uuid "81ec4ac7-c58c-54fd-b25d-7a69d7cee835" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71e3d4ed-542d-5a05-ad15-08f8d9b28925" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71e3d4ed-542d-5a05-ad15-08f8d9b28925" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305383} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1d65a68-556e-5cd7-a21b-c05da35d7021" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f84e8c3-0aa3-5680-ba44-b0d4f51527fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-181695" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-1,\\frac{1}{3}}$ given below.\n\n${-1,\\frac{1}{3}}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,3{q}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$q\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $q\\in Q$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(q).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${q}_{1}=-1$ and ${q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(q) & =a(q-{q}_{1})(q-{q}_{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (q-(-1))(q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3(q+1)(q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3({q}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3{q}^{2}+2q-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{-1,\\frac{1}{3}}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,3{q}^{2}+2q-1=0}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9df722a8-2db6-5bb8-a69c-b81b33037ab2" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Given Set Using a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d01f687-8a0c-58a4-9d67-1d16caba6c6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195945} {:answer/id #uuid "3aeb5059-9e9d-5377-ba3f-e238cb0bd3af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195946} {:answer/id #uuid "665b400c-0bbe-5234-8b41-b385f197622c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "665b400c-0bbe-5234-8b41-b385f197622c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195947} :answer-field/id #uuid "a837f807-51e1-5d8a-a302-8e17816924de" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195944} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd106a54-d58e-5b0a-9155-eaced26adb5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305386} {:answer/id #uuid "13720b7a-d92a-53d8-914d-33a11814d040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305387} {:answer/id #uuid "d63876f1-6bca-56f0-9f96-ed3512295346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {3}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305388} {:answer/id #uuid "0239a17d-f98b-5656-9f43-4187f25618ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {3}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305389} {:answer/id #uuid "a66f7219-c10b-5e9d-8453-fdae270140e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13720b7a-d92a-53d8-914d-33a11814d040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305387} :answer-field/id #uuid "962a54a0-8363-579c-a8ee-87d876aed503" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a35af51-a0e2-50d0-bbd3-1c0dc3bc52aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-183328" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={…,3,6,12,24,48,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=6$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {3}^{n}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,3,\\,6,\\,12,\\,24,\\,48,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{12} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=6,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={3\\cdot {2}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f49ef1c2-06de-597c-bf4d-6d613989987e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Set Using a Conditional Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09142362-8a96-59f4-8448-554e02879f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305393} {:answer/id #uuid "05d176b3-cf36-5301-92fd-9a245bc0b692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305394} {:answer/id #uuid "1cea76d9-237f-5854-8775-a6487c063a59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305395} {:answer/id #uuid "61bb82f8-d8d4-52cf-9d26-dcb0169a56ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09142362-8a96-59f4-8448-554e02879f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305393} :answer-field/id #uuid "02d02695-280a-58a3-ace1-a4bcf19c8392" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305392} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a4a87b-e691-58df-ae24-65044189619b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305398} {:answer/id #uuid "0b5be72d-4c33-5e2f-ab35-ee2336695357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305399} {:answer/id #uuid "e63f0463-9a4b-56f9-8076-e9de032f256f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e63f0463-9a4b-56f9-8076-e9de032f256f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305400} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8867894-5c52-5f9c-8461-5d7e81ece3e3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "105cef8d-b86a-5101-bcde-0428f1f7bf15" :question/math-academy-id "q-183663" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={5,6,7,…}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nQ\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers greater than or equal to $5.$\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x\\ge 5}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:x\\ge 5}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $x>4.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x>4},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x>4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305401 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f49ef1c2-06de-597c-bf4d-6d613989987e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Set Using a Conditional Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02cc176e-39dc-50d7-97cc-ff45c5f27280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305403} {:answer/id #uuid "84d602b7-b844-5c63-b226-03948212f336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305404} {:answer/id #uuid "eb60b1a3-836e-55ee-8c3a-45ffca228b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305405} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb727ea-5342-5e06-aec7-bf7117946b87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02cc176e-39dc-50d7-97cc-ff45c5f27280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305403} :answer-field/id #uuid "94d2e431-98c7-5711-9591-dab112453ca7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a8869e6-c527-5cf2-827f-fde19e7f0237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305408} {:answer/id #uuid "125ab8be-fc26-5bb1-a5ae-4b574ed8bf89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305409} {:answer/id #uuid "322909a0-8e3d-5c2f-a3b5-740141a06d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "322909a0-8e3d-5c2f-a3b5-740141a06d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305410} :answer-field/id #uuid "23af84fd-10ce-5aa0-83be-0febb5f