wer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305412} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b347f7ce-5a01-5667-86da-967c9434c912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305418} {:answer/id #uuid "11904368-21c1-5c22-9287-0905c57c83c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305419} {:answer/id #uuid "03fb4937-84fb-5d3a-b14d-f4b93b90e179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b347f7ce-5a01-5667-86da-967c9434c912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305418} :answer-field/id #uuid "3954dbd2-636d-5cc4-a087-6916faf13d6d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4a3efeb6-13c0-531b-9e5f-bba9b43b00d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183689" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={1,2,3,…,29}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nR\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers less than or equal to $29.$\n\nIn other words, $S$ contains all natural numbers less than $30,$ *excluding* $30.$\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as \n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x<30}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,0<x<30}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $x\\le 29.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x\\le 29},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:1\\le x\\le 29}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f49ef1c2-06de-597c-bf4d-6d613989987e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Set Using a Conditional Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fi