id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1d88cc5-5f34-51c6-bb45-73abd209e524" :question/math-academy-id "q-183765" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={...,3,6,9,12,15,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=3$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\nn+2\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9,\\,12,\\,15,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =3 \\\\  & =6-3 \\\\  & =9-6 \\\\  & =12-9 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=3,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =3+(n-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={3n\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c5b3eb6-187f-5f16-a32e-66b0842adfe9" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Given Set Using an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2436ddd-c1de-5175-8635-998cf67bcb6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3n-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305502} {:answer/id #uuid "297270af-99d1-5f36-9e1f-f76bf9240ce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305503} {:answer/id #uuid "8836f71f-9319-5638-ae89-33d65e227aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5n+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305504} {:answer/id #uuid "01b9a7e2-1e50-5cb6-bd53-fb58ea8fdb95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5n-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305505} {:answer/id #uuid "345a417e-507a-5433-b915-ef5175d4932c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5n+2" :db/id #edb/ref 175921863055