\\,-19,\\,-14,\\,-9,\\,-4,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =5 \\\\  & =-19-(-24) \\\\  & =-14-(-19) \\\\  & =-9-(-14) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=-4,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =-4+(n-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-4+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={5n-9\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c5b3eb6-187f-5f16-a32e-66b0842adfe9" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Given Set Using an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3256e33d-8418-599d-ad4e-cfccba1579a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2n-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305515} {:answer/id #uuid "3fd58850-5095-5ef4-9fc9-7d6f56b2e213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305516} {:answer/id #uuid "95cb9f09-94e1-57f1-86ae-ca1a89da53a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305517} {:answer/id #uuid "680d1a94-8828-51d8-af69-a9354c07042a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4n+21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305518} {:answer/id #uuid "1fcc61af-b91f-5516-8039-1dc6aa7abd03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4n-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fcc61af-b91f-5516-8039-1dc6aa7abd03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4n-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305519} :answer-field/id #uuid "46033f14-2542-5aae-9267-411cdd1f7688" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305514} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "621