\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,1,\\,4,\\,16,\\,64,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =4 \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{4} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=4,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {4}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {4}^{n}\\cdot {4}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}\\cdot {4}^{n} \\\\  & ={4}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={{4}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9df722a8-2db6-5bb8-a69c-b81b33037ab2" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Given Set Using a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "980e1a60-6340-5a50-a4ed-7663f57f58eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305548} {:answer/id #uuid "d88d1ef5-4fc9-519c-aa05-d082c7fdfde7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {3}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305549} {:answer/id #uuid "51316c81-d579-5604-8318-63c5605a90d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305550} {:answer/id #uuid "30572f73-0309-5301-805f-a21ba85ef989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {3}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d88d1ef5-4fc9-519c-aa05-d082c7fdfde7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {3}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305549} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe119c86-cfa9-5f4c-be54-de57f7523e7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305547} 