 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10d6db30-bad7-59d8-aa8b-37df74b83a6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183795" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={4,24,144,864,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\n6\\cdot {4}^{n}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n4,\\,24,\\,144,\\,864,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =6 \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{864}{144} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {6}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {6}^{n}\\cdot {6}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {6}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {6}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N}\n$$"}]}
